Limitless XYZ 3D Printer (patent pending 2026)

A small printer taht can print any size object.

No phisical constrains on 3D printing size (just by material/shape/gravity and space to buid object).
OmniPrinter that can print entire skyscrapers, La Tour Eiffel at 1:1 scale (10 years print) or any other big object.
I prints on plastic (extrusion PLA) but it could also print metals (electrodeposition) or cement (ultrafast-dry-cement)
Pint head and printer OmniBot or OmniPrinter are scalable. Small robot to print smaller but detailed prints with 0.1-0.3 layer height
and bigger OmniBot for bigger prints like cement buildings or metalic structures like skyscrapers.

The patented tecnic consists of a omnidireccional robot with one or more printheads of filament deposition or block position
or any type of extrusion, deposition, melting, anything actually that can put material.

The core concept is not the omnidireccional robot nor the deposition or placing material element or printheat.

The true genius of the idea (the patented part) how to make a small printer become a Limitless 3D Printer Omnirobot.

